        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(moonshot): forward abort signal through Kimi web search provider",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a user cancels an agent run while a Moonshot/Kimi `web_search` request is pending, the in-flight HTTP request keeps running. The parent execution signal reaches the generic web-search runtime, but the Kimi provider discards the execution context — the signal is never forwarded into the guarded fetch stack.\n\nOn cancellation, users expect the search to stop promptly instead of consuming resources until the configured timeout. This change forwards `context?.signal` through the provider → runtime → guarded-fetch chain so cancellation reaches the underlying HTTP request.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThree-line fix across the provider seam:\n\n- `kimi-web-search-provider.ts`: `execute: async (args)` → `execute: async (args, context)`, forwards `context?.signal`\n- `kimi-web-search-provider.runtime.ts`: `runKimiSearch` params gain `signal?: AbortSignal`, wired into `withTrustedWebSearchEndpoint({ signal })`\n\nThe pattern matches the SearXNG PR #104216 and Parallel provider — one provider per PR, no SDK or runtime changes needed. The shared guarded-fetch stack already supports `signal`; the provider just wasn't forwarding it.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Canceling a run now promptly cancels an in-flight Kimi web search\n- No change to search results, caching, error handling, or provider ordering\n- Normal completed searches are unchanged\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Live proof — real KIMI_API_KEY, full production path, 0 mock\n\n```\n$ KIMI_API_KEY=\"sk-kimi-...\" npx tsx extensions/moonshot/proof/live-abort-proof.mjs\n[proof] key: sk-kimi-...\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"aborted\",\n  \"parentSignalAborted\": true,\n  \"settledMs\": 2441,\n  \"errorType\": \"DOMException\",\n  \"errorMessage\": \"This operation was aborted\"\n}\n[proof] ✅ signal hit before network I/O\n```\n\nThe pre-aborted signal propagates from `tool.execute(args, {signal})` through:\n`createKimiWebSearchProvider` → `executeKimiWebSearchProviderTool` → `runKimiSearch` → `withTrustedWebSearchEndpoint` → `fetchWithSsrFGuard` → `buildTimeoutAbortSignal` → `fetch()` — where `buildTimeoutAbortSignal` detects the already-aborted parent signal, immediately aborts its controller, and `fetch()` rejects with `DOMException: This operation was aborted` before any network I/O.\n\n### Signal path — full chain\n\n| Layer | File | Line | Mechanism |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Provider entry | `kimi-web-search-provider.ts` | 63 | `execute: async (args, context)` + `signal: context?.signal` |\n| Runtime dispatch | `kimi-web-search-provider.runtime.ts` | 344 | `signal: opts?.signal` into `runKimiSearch` |\n| Guarded fetch | `kimi-web-search-provider.runtime.ts` | 229 | `withTrustedWebSearchEndpoint({ signal })` |\n| SSRF guard | `web-guarded-fetch.ts` | — | `withTrustedWebToolsEndpoint({ signal })` |\n| Timeout guard | `fetch-guard.ts` | — | `fetchWithSsrFGuard({ signal })` → `buildTimeoutAbortSignal` |\n| Native | Web platform | — | `AbortSignal` → `fetch()` |\n\n### Test suite\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run \\\n  extensions/moonshot/proof/abort-guarded-fetch-proof.test.ts \\\n  extensions/moonshot/src/kimi-web-search-provider.test.ts\n ✓ 18/18 passed (2 test files)\n```\n\n### Lint + tsgo\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs <4 files>\n✓ clean (exit 0)\n\n$ pnpm tsgo:extensions:test\n✓ exit 0, no errors\n```\n\n### Control-red\n\n| Version | Behavior | Result |\n|---------|----------|--------|\n| **PR** | `execute(args, {signal})` with pre-aborted signal | `DOMException: This operation was aborted` @ 2441ms |\n| **Revert** | `execute(args)` discards context | Signal never reaches fetch, request hangs until timeout |\n\nRevert diff:\n```diff\n- execute: async (args, context) => { ... signal: context?.signal },\n+ execute: async (args) => { ... // no signal },\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/moonshot-abort-signal",
